-- Version 1 -> 2. Removes the hand-rolled schema version table.
--
-- `schema_meta` was Phase 1 wiring, written before there was a migration
-- mechanism for a version number to mean anything to. Nothing in the app
-- ever read it; only a smoke test did. Leaving it beside SQLite's own
-- `user_version` -- which is what SQLDelight actually reads to decide
-- whether to migrate -- leaves two versioning mechanisms in one database
-- and makes the decoy the more obvious of the two.
--
-- It is also why this migration exists at this point in the project rather
-- than later. The mechanism has to be proved by a real schema change that
-- a real database survives, and a mechanism first exercised by the change
-- that needed it is a mechanism first exercised on a referee's phone.
DROP TABLE schema_meta;
